// TODO before the first deploy. The build itself no longer needs WordPress —
// every WordPress-backed route is `prerender = false` — so everything here is
// about what has to be true at request time.
//
// 1. Secrets, both read at runtime and deliberately absent from .env.production:
//    `npx wrangler secret put OPENAI_API_KEY`
//    `npx wrangler secret put QUERY_LOG_SECRET`, with the value of
//    QUERY_LOG_SECRET in the demo WordPress wp-config.php.
// 2. The demo backend, https://regista.regista-demo.net (xserver, not uploaded
//    as of 2026-10-14), must match local: theme regista-hp, which registers the
//    belief / method / project / member / note post types, WPGraphQL + ACF +
//    wpgraphql-acf + wpgraphql-blocks, Yoast + add-wpgraphql-seo (the page
//    template queries `seo`), and both mu-plugins (regista-query-log,
//    regista-interest).
// 3. Check `POST /graphql` from outside the host: the Worker runs with
//    global_fetch_strictly_public, so no private addresses and no basic auth,
//    and an xserver WAF rule may block the POST.
// 4. SEO, once the backend is up: set `site` in astro.config.mjs, query Yoast's
//    `seo { fullHead }` and inject it in CommonHead, running it through
//    utils/replaceUrls so canonical and og:url point at the Astro domain
//    rather than at regista.regista-demo.net. Add robots.txt and a sitemap.
{
	"$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-09-11",
	"compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "global_fetch_strictly_public"],
	"name": "regista-astro-hp",
	"main": "@astrojs/cloudflare/entrypoints/server",
	"assets": {
		"directory": "./dist",
		"binding": "ASSETS"
	},
	"observability": {
		"enabled": true
	}
}